    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d32-a5">

                <pb facs="0123" n="51" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg51"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 5 in No.
                    20.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Coban</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-09-21"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 21,
                        1882</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#italic">To the Minister of War:</hi></p>
                <p>At this moment I have received a courier from the prefect of Peten, recommending
                    the following telegram to be sent to you:</p>
                <p>“On the 15th instant one of the spies sent to the frontier of Campeche returned,
                    stating that forces from that state to the number of 200 men have invaded the
                    department and are marching upon this capital.”</p>
                <p>I await your orders,</p>
                <closer><signed>LUIS MOLINA.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
